[{:db/id 17592186198417 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-ae31463b-0937-5dcb-a149-ee8482b71924" "question-4a051470-22b3-5741-85c9-94876b2374fa"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186281677 :question/problem "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 3\\}.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the origin." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-ae31463b-0937-5dcb-a149-ee8482b71924" :question/id #uuid "ae31463b-0937-5dcb-a149-ee8482b71924" :question/math-academy-id "q-163579" :question/problem "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 4,\\,\\,2\\le y\\le 5\\}.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the $y$-axis." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nThe moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function.\n\nThe area of the rectangular plate $D$ is $A=3\\cdot 3=9.$ Since the plate has uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{M}{9}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{9}{\\int }_{2}^{5}{\\int }_{1}^{4}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{9}{\\int }_{2}^{5}{[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}]}_{1}^{4}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{9}{\\int }_{2}^{5}(\\frac{64}{3}-\\frac{1}{3})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{9}{\\int }_{2}^{5}21\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{7M}{3}{\\int }_{2}^{5}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{7M}{3}[y]_{2}^{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{7M}{3}(5-2) \\\\  & =7M.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{R}_{y}^{2}=7\\,⇒\\,{R}_{y}=\\sqrt{7}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-02ef48a6-5de2-5aeb-b94d-50e269438d16"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-02ef48a6-5de2-5aeb-b94d-50e269438d16" :answer-field/id #uuid "02ef48a6-5de2-5aeb-b94d-50e269438d16" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-9bbfff91-ca90-559f-ae5d-5fd328a1f1e9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2ca9c9b8-05e4-5eb3-8122-ad72c6a359f7" "answer-1e358496-a583-59a6-b4e0-5fcf99d9cafa" "answer-9bbfff91-ca90-559f-ae5d-5fd328a1f1e9" "answer-688f7ffe-b0fd-57c9-821e-0495e33a6fae" "answer-bb7abb37-0de9-58cb-8a76-9f11aa3adea3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2ca9c9b8-05e4-5eb3-8122-ad72c6a359f7" :answer/id #uuid "2ca9c9b8-05e4-5eb3-8122-ad72c6a359f7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1e358496-a583-59a6-b4e0-5fcf99d9cafa" :answer/id #uuid "1e358496-a583-59a6-b4e0-5fcf99d9cafa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9bbfff91-ca90-559f-ae5d-5fd328a1f1e9" :answer/id #uuid "9bbfff91-ca90-559f-ae5d-5fd328a1f1e9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-688f7ffe-b0fd-57c9-821e-0495e33a6fae" :answer/id #uuid "688f7ffe-b0fd-57c9-821e-0495e33a6fae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{17}{5}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bb7abb37-0de9-58cb-8a76-9f11aa3adea3" :answer/id #uuid "bb7abb37-0de9-58cb-8a76-9f11aa3adea3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{21}{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198664 :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nThe moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function. The region $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le x\\}.\n$$\n\nHence, the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{x}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{3}{4}My\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{x}{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{[\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}{y}^{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{4}{[\\frac{1}{10}{x}^{5}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{4}\\cdot \\frac{16}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{12M}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of gyration about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{y} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{12M}{5}\\cdot \\frac{1}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{12}{5}} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{\\frac{3}{5}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-4a051470-22b3-5741-85c9-94876b2374fa" :question/id #uuid "4a051470-22b3-5741-85c9-94876b2374fa" :question/math-academy-id "q-163606" :question/problem "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 4,\\,\\,1\\le y\\le 3\\}.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the origin." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nThe moment of inertia about the origin is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function.\n\nThe area of the rectangular plate $D$ is $A=3\\cdot 2=6.$ Since the plate has uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{M}{6}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{0} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}{\\int }_{1}^{3}{\\int }_{1}^{4}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}{\\int }_{1}^{3}{[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}+x{y}^{2}]}_{x=1}^{x=4}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}{\\int }_{1}^{3}(\\frac{64}{3}+4{y}^{2}-\\frac{1}{3}-{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}{\\int }_{1}^{3}21+3{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}{[21y+{y}^{3}]}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}(63+27-21-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}\\cdot 68 \\\\  & =\\frac{34M}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{R}_{0}^{2}=\\frac{34}{3}\\,⇒\\,{R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{34}{3}}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-364a1bfa-3c03-5519-b8cb-713056748a8b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-364a1bfa-3c03-5519-b8cb-713056748a8b" :answer-field/id #uuid "364a1bfa-3c03-5519-b8cb-713056748a8b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-61c6c170-edd9-5422-8928-2559bb6d8200" :answer-field/choices ["answer-aed2bb04-ea3b-5b55-b733-92f0f589ec24" "answer-4e9fa620-f201-58e2-aec9-4998cb5b396c" "answer-020395fa-1c94-56f4-b0cf-6b542584a05e" "answer-61c6c170-edd9-5422-8928-2559bb6d8200" "answer-7f05bbf6-f47e-5bba-ae07-b44dd179c296"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-aed2bb04-ea3b-5b55-b733-92f0f589ec24" :answer/id #uuid "aed2bb04-ea3b-5b55-b733-92f0f589ec24" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{17}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4e9fa620-f201-58e2-aec9-4998cb5b396c" :answer/id #uuid "4e9fa620-f201-58e2-aec9-4998cb5b396c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{17}}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-020395fa-1c94-56f4-b0cf-6b542584a05e" :answer/id #uuid "020395fa-1c94-56f4-b0cf-6b542584a05e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{21}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-61c6c170-edd9-5422-8928-2559bb6d8200" :answer/id #uuid "61c6c170-edd9-5422-8928-2559bb6d8200" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{34}{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7f05bbf6-f47e-5bba-ae07-b44dd179c296" :answer/id #uuid "7f05bbf6-f47e-5bba-ae07-b44dd179c296" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{61}{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198665 :question/problem "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,4\\le y\\le 6\\}.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the $y$-axis." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "activity-74cd288a-6d4e-5649-a0a3-fd1f66ef23c9" :activity/id #uuid "74cd288a-6d4e-5649-a0a3-fd1f66ef23c9" :activity/title "Calculating the Radius of Gyration of a Plane Lamina" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186050741 :activity/course 17592186046660 :activity/steps ["step-0e7b7881-d766-59e5-9ac2-17b4c071226f" "step-ce124292-03a7-514d-bbf3-a753805c4055" "step-c02d457b-f21d-50f7-b09e-291abfa68047" "step-f1544047-bb8b-536b-b9d7-9b50cf101d4e" "step-512ba0cc-ab8c-5fb2-8948-44914ec8fb98"] :activity/first-step "step-0e7b7881-d766-59e5-9ac2-17b4c071226f" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-0e7b7881-d766-59e5-9ac2-17b4c071226f" :step/id #uuid "0e7b7881-d766-59e5-9ac2-17b4c071226f" :step/content 17592186281677 :step/next "step-ce124292-03a7-514d-bbf3-a753805c4055" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-ce124292-03a7-514d-bbf3-a753805c4055" :step/id #uuid "ce124292-03a7-514d-bbf3-a753805c4055" :step/content "question-ae31463b-0937-5dcb-a149-ee8482b71924" :step/next "step-c02d457b-f21d-50f7-b09e-291abfa68047" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-c02d457b-f21d-50f7-b09e-291abfa68047" :step/id #uuid "c02d457b-f21d-50f7-b09e-291abfa68047" :step/content 17592186198664 :step/next "step-f1544047-bb8b-536b-b9d7-9b50cf101d4e" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-f1544047-bb8b-536b-b9d7-9b50cf101d4e" :step/id #uuid "f1544047-bb8b-536b-b9d7-9b50cf101d4e" :step/content "question-4a051470-22b3-5741-85c9-94876b2374fa" :step/next "step-512ba0cc-ab8c-5fb2-8948-44914ec8fb98" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-512ba0cc-ab8c-5fb2-8948-44914ec8fb98" :step/id #uuid "512ba0cc-ab8c-5fb2-8948-44914ec8fb98" :step/content 17592186198665 